  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Sweden's greatest warship sank after sailing 1,300 metres. The crowds on the Stockholm quay were still waving at her.",
        "visual_query": "stockholm harbour old sailing ship",
        "visual_fallback": "harbour quay"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Vasa carried sixty-four guns, forty-eight of them twenty-four pounders, stacked across two decks. Enormous weight, carried much too high.",
        "visual_query": "bronze cannon wooden gun deck",
        "visual_fallback": "bronze cannon"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They already knew. Thirty men ran back and forth across her deck to test her, and the admiral stopped it after three passes.",
        "visual_query": "swedish naval shipyard wooden hull",
        "visual_fallback": "wooden hull"
      },
      {
        "narration": "On the tenth of August a gust caught her. She leaned, and water came straight in through the open lower gun ports.",
        "visual_query": "baltic sea grey choppy water",
        "visual_fallback": "choppy sea"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The Baltic is too brackish for shipworm, so nothing ate her. She came back up in 1961, after 333 years, nearly whole.",
        "visual_query": "preserved wooden warship museum hall",
        "visual_fallback": "ship museum"
      }
